{
    "background_story": "In ancient Greek mythology, Archie was a demigod with the powers of Argus, the all-seeing giant. Born with 100 eyes, Archie possessed unparalleled vigilance and insight. He roamed the mortal realm, using his extraordinary abilities to protect the innocent and vanquish evil. With his eyes ever-watchful, Archie could see through deception and detect hidden dangers. His nickname 'The Guardian' spread far and wide, striking fear into the hearts of wrongdoers. One fateful night, Archie foiled a plot to steal the magical ambrosia, saving the gods' favorite snack from falling into mortal hands. As a reward, Zeus granted Archie a place among the stars, where his celestial eyes continue to watch over the world, ever vigilant and always just.",
